  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would disrupt the uniform building line and built form of a prominent terrace row within a Neighbourhood Centre and would appear as a discordant addition which fails to appear subordinate to the original building.&nbsp;As a result, it fails to respect or reflect the character and appearance of the original building, terrace row and wider area, causing undue harm to each of these as well as to the street scene along Reede Road. The proposal therefore fails to accord with the following policies which seek to ensure that development proposals are of a high quality design which pays regard to the local character:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, 2024);Policies D4 &amp; D8 of the London Plan (March 2021);Policies SP2, DMD1 &amp; DMD3 of the LBBD’s Local Plan (September 2024)"
  ],
